<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank said on Friday it allocated 2.97 billion guilders to the money market under a seven-day special advances pact at an unchanged rate of 2.50 percent.</p>
<p>Individual banks' applications of up to 3.5 billion guilders were met for 11.5 percent. No subscriptions were awarded above that level.</p>
<p>The pact replaces a seven-day facility of 5.14 billion guilders which expired today.</p>
